WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.870 align:start position:0%
 
ted  monday officially marks the start of a  brand new school year for clark county  school district students teachers have  already reported back to the classroom  while the district is working to fill  about 2 100 staffing positions the  school year runs through may 22nd of  next year  so because of that we have a very  special cool at school story tonight for  parents as nate tannenbaum explains  getting to the first bell in one piece  is the most important part of the day  taryn breen from the road equity  alliance project wants to cut down on  the crazy traffic crowding of so many  kids getting dropped off at the same  time the less congestion around the  school the safer every child is she adds  not living within walking distance could  be a blessing in disguise if parents  would even park two or three blocks away  and walk their children in from there  what a big difference it would make the  bonuses you get to spend extra time with  your kid and how could that be bad  drivers can't let their guard down once  they're away from any flashing lights in  the immediate vicinity of any campus in  fact brain urges extra attention when  there might be kids on streets near  schools now you've got them crossing 45  mile an hour traffic instead of 25 mile  an hour traffic so you got to pay  attention to those school crossing zones  as much as the actual school zone and  aaron suggests that while the  sentimental urge may be strong as you  send your kid off  maybe try being a little bit of a nag  instead in place of saying i love you as  you leave the house in the morning  remind them put your seatbelt on  make eye contact with drivers where's  your bike helmet just that that one  final thing that could literally save  their life  we will of course have back to school  coverage all day monday here on eight  news now and of course on our website  eightnewsnow.com and if you know  something that's cool at school  let us know cool at school is under the  community tab on our website or email us  coolant school at 8newsnow.com

